WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
A goal you can count: gaps and good decisions.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.350
Dewi wants a scholarship abroad. On her wall there is one line: improve my English.

3
00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:15.280
That is a wish. You cannot calculate a gap for a wish.

4
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:23.580
A solid goal has three parts. What: a language test score of 6.5. By when: the first of March. And under which conditions: without leaving her part-time job.

5
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.900
Now the gap is a number. Today she scores 5.5. At her current pace she reaches 5.9. The gap is 0.6.

6
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:39.290
She stacks her plan as a pyramid. On top, the conclusion: I can close the gap by the first of March. Underneath, the reasons: writing, listening, speaking. Writing and listening hold. Speaking does not improve when she practises alone.

7
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:45.770
If the reasons do not add up, there is no plan yet. She needs a speaking partner.

8
00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:54.190
For speaking she has two options. A plain list of pros and cons would favour the cheaper course. So she lists criteria that come from the goal, and gives them weights.

9
00:00:54.590 --> 00:01:00.450
Weighted, the online tutor wins: sixteen to eleven.

10
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:06.320
Before she commits, she challenges her own conclusion. She asks a senior who won the same scholarship. One conversation gives her a fact that a week of worrying never did.

11
00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:13.720
A goal without a gap you can count is a wish. Criteria come from the goal. Weights come from the criteria.

12
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.520
Now it is your turn. Write one goal with what, by when and conditions. Then calculate the gap.
